---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE, LEGAL_ENTITY, CONTACT_EMAIL, EFFECTIVE_DATE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title={`Privacy Policy — ${SITE_TITLE}`}
			description={`How ${SITE_TITLE} handles subscriber data.`}
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />

		<main class="wrap">
			<article class="prose">
				<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
				<p class="updated">Effective date: {EFFECTIVE_DATE}</p>

				<p>
					This policy explains what {LEGAL_ENTITY}, trading as {SITE_TITLE} (&ldquo;we,&rdquo;
					&ldquo;us&rdquo;), collects from subscribers to The Weekend Dugout (the
					&ldquo;Service&rdquo;), why we collect it, and who else touches it. It should be read
					alongside our <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>.
				</p>

				<h2>1. What we collect</h2>
				<p>We collect only what is needed to bill you and deliver the digest:</p>
				<ul>
					<li>
						<strong>Email address.</strong> Provided by you at signup and used as your delivery
						address and account identifier.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Subscription status.</strong> Whether your subscription is active, past due, or
						cancelled, and the associated billing period.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Delivery events.</strong> Standard email operational data such as whether a
						message was delivered, bounced, or unsubscribed.
					</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					<strong>We do not collect or store your payment card details.</strong> Card data is entered
					directly with Stripe and never reaches our systems.
				</p>

				<h2>2. What we do not do</h2>
				<ul>
					<li>We do not sell, rent, or trade subscriber email addresses.</li>
					<li>We do not share your address with advertisers or list brokers.</li>
					<li>We do not use your data to build profiles for third-party marketing.</li>
				</ul>

				<h2>3. Service providers</h2>
				<p>
					We rely on third-party processors to operate the Service. Each handles your data under its
					own privacy terms:
				</p>
				<ul>
					<li>
						<strong>Stripe</strong> — payment processing, subscription management, and tax
						calculation. Stripe is the system of record for billing and holds your payment details.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Make.com</strong> — the automation platform that assembles and triggers digest
						delivery.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Our email delivery provider</strong> — transmits the digest to your inbox.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Cloudflare</strong> — hosts this website and provides standard network security
						and abuse protection.
					</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					We may add or change providers as the Service evolves and will update this policy when we
					do.
				</p>

				<h2>4. Automated content generation</h2>
				<p>
					Digest content is produced with automated systems, including AI models that summarize and
					classify public filings. These systems process the <em>filings</em>, not your personal
					data. Your email address is not included in prompts sent to any AI provider.
				</p>

				<h2>5. Website analytics and cookies</h2>
				<p>
					This site does not set advertising or tracking cookies and does not run third-party
					analytics. Our host may log standard request data (IP address, user agent, timestamp) for
					security and abuse prevention. If we add analytics later, we will update this policy first.
				</p>

				<h2>6. Retention</h2>
				<p>
					We keep your email address for as long as your subscription is active. After cancellation,
					we retain it only as long as needed for records, tax, and dispute-resolution purposes, and
					then delete it. Billing records held by Stripe are retained per Stripe&rsquo;s own schedule
					and applicable financial recordkeeping law.
				</p>

				<h2>7. Your choices</h2>
				<ul>
					<li>
						<strong>Unsubscribe</strong> from delivery using the link in the footer of any issue.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Cancel billing</strong> at any time; access continues through the period already
						paid, per the <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Request access or deletion</strong> of the personal data we hold by emailing us
						at the address below. We will respond within a reasonable period.
					</li>
				</ul>

				<h2>8. Security</h2>
				<p>
					We limit stored personal data to the minimum described above and rely on established
					providers for payment and delivery infrastructure. No method of transmission or storage is
					perfectly secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.
				</p>

				<h2>9. Children</h2>
				<p>
					The Service is not directed to anyone under 18, and we do not knowingly collect data from
					children.
				</p>

				<h2>10. Changes</h2>
				<p>
					We may update this policy; material changes will be communicated via the Service. Continued
					use after the effective date constitutes acceptance.
				</p>

				<h2>11. Contact</h2>
				<p>
					{LEGAL_ENTITY} · 11907 Sun Valley Drive, Fort Washington, MD 20744 ·
					<a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>
				</p>
			</article>
		</main>

		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	.prose p,
	.prose li {
		font-size: 0.95rem;
	}
</style>
